{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Vanessa Makes a New Friend", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "A Date With Marco", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 6, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Writing a Descriptive Paragraph", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you write a descriptive paragraph, use different types of sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "There are four sentence types:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Simple</span></br> Simple sentences do not have conjunctions (and, but, or). </br><span class=\"italic\">Example: Marco climbed the mountain.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Compound</span></br> Compound sentences have two statements that are connected by a conjunction.</br> <span class=\"italic\">Example: Vanessa waited in the parking lot and Marco had a coffee.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Complex</span></br> A complex sentence has one complete sentence (independent clause) and at least one incomplete sentence (dependent clause).</br> The two clauses are connected by a word like <span class=\"italic\">which, who, although, if,</span> or<span class=\"italic\"> since</span>. </br><span class=\"italic\">Example: If you turn left at the intersection, you will see the mountain ahead of you.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Compound - Complex</span></br> A compound-complex sentence contains at least one dependent clause and more than one independent clause.</br> <span class=\"italic\">Example: Marco, who arrived last month, met his co-worker, and then he decided to take her on a date.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "&nbsp;", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Past Tense and Past Continuous Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You make the Past Continuous tense by using the Past tense of the verb <span class=\"strong\">to be</span> and the -ing form of the verb. </br></br>You use the Past Continuous tense to talk about:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol> <li>something which continued before and after another action </br>Example: <span class=\"italic\">Marco and Vanessa were climbing up the mountain  when they heard a noise in the bush.</span></li> <li>something that happened before and after a time period </br>Example: <span class=\"italic\">It was eight o'clock. I was writing a letter.</span> <li> something that continued for some time</br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">My knee was aching.</li> <li>something that was happening again and again </br>Example: <span class=\"italic\">I was jogging every day, three times a day.</span></li></ol>", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "parking lot ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an area outside a building for parking cars and  trucks", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Vanessa waited in the parking lot.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you are doing outside activities.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to bother", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cause someone to feel worried, annoyed or concerned", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Vanessa was a little bothered.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "tender ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very loving and gentle; showing affection and love for someone or something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Marco was very tender with the bird.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "angel", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a spiritual being that is a messenger from God", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He is such an angel!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to struggle", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to try very hard to do, achieve, or deal with something that is difficult or that causes problems", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Vanessa struggled to keep up with Marco.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to wind", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to follow a series of curves and turns", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We were winding our way to the top.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "wing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a part of an animal's body that is used for flying or gliding", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The bird's wing was broken.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob08aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "catch my breath", "type": "name"}, {"content": "use when you find it difficult to breathe", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Vanessa needed to catch her breath.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob08aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Write a 75-word descriptive paragraph about a friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Include information about their appearance and personality.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use simple, compound and complex sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use paragraph structure.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I write a descriptive paragraph about a friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use proper sentence structure.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I proofread my work.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn5le06ob08re2img06.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn5le06ob08re2img06.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "Subject Line - A Date To Remember</br></br>Hey Sally,</p>I had to tell you about my date last Saturday.</p>Marco and I went for a hike up Table Ridge Mountain. I was waiting in the parking lot for half an hour before he arrived. I was a little bothered, but when he showed up with a single, red rose, I forgave him immediately."}, {"image": "engenn5le06ob08re2img01.jpg", "time": "23000", "id": 2, "text": "Marco's so sweet. Have I told you how athletic he is too?  I'm sure he must spend a lot of time in the gym.  He was taking two steps at a time while I struggled to catch my breath. We were winding our way to the top when we heard a strange noise in the bushes. There, we found a blue jay with a broken wing."}, {"image": "engenn5le06ob08re2img05.jpg", "time": "46000", "id": 3, "text": "Marco took off his shirt and wrapped up the bird.  We decided to head back down the mountain to find a vet.  Sally, he was so tender and gentle with the injured animal. What an angel!</p>Chat soon,</br>\nVanessa"}], "audiosrc": "engenn5le06ob08re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le06ob08re2img06.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}, {"templ